{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Gad, a troop shall troop upon him.</b> He praised him for valor and said that he would have many wars and troops would come upon him — <b>but he shall troop upon their heel,</b> that is, in the end he shall advance with his troop against them and prevail; or the meaning of והוא יגוד עקב is that he shall cut them off in the end, from the language of גדו אילנא (they cut the tree). And Moses our teacher, peace be upon him, interpreted this verse, as he said (Deuteronomy 33:20): ״ברוך מרחיב גד כלביא שכן וטרף זרוע אף קדקד״." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> ״והוא יגוד עקב״ — when Jacob saw Samson, who would come from Dan, he said, ״לישועתך קויתי ה׳״ — 'this one will not bring the redemption'; but from Gad, ״והוא יגוד עקב״ — he who comes בעקב (at the heel), as it is said (Malachi 3:23): ״הנה אנכי שולח לכם את אליה הנביא״ — he is from Gad. Thus far in Bereshit Rabbah."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:37.146719338Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}